{%- comment -%}
  customer-privacy-bar — CANONICAL cookie-consent snippet (2026-08-25, P1 cookie-bar rip).

  REPLACES: custom `pn-consent.js` / `pn-consent.css` / `cookie-consent.liquid` per-theme
  implementations. On penelope these produced 10 of 75 commits and a persistent vision-judge
  false positive ("chrome-on-brand", ×4 recurrences) that cost ~13% of build time.

  HOW IT WORKS.
  Shopify's Customer Privacy API renders a compliant consent banner NATIVELY when the merchant
  enables it in Shopify Admin → Settings → Customer privacy → Cookie banner. The theme does not
  paint the bar itself; it only exposes the `window.Shopify.customerPrivacy` API for downstream
  consent-gated features (analytics, marketing pixels).

  ADMIN SETUP (one-time, per store):
    Shopify Admin → Settings → Customer privacy → Cookie banner → Enable → pick region + style.
    Docs: https://shopify.dev/docs/api/customer-privacy

  IF YOU NEED consent-gated custom code:
    document.addEventListener('visitorConsentCollected', (e) => {
      if (window.Shopify.customerPrivacy.userCanBeTracked()) {
        // fire analytics / marketing pixels here
      }
    });

  ANTI-PATTERN reminder (Yash / ink lesson pack, 2026-08-25):
    Do NOT hand-roll a consent bar to work around a vision-judge false-positive on the native
    one. The FP is fixed by re-tuning lens-rubrics/home.json chrome exclusions, not by wrapping
    Shopify's bar in custom Liquid. Every custom implementation reintroduces the debt.

  RENDERING: this snippet emits NOTHING to the DOM. It exists as a documentation anchor and a
  placement marker in layout/theme.liquid so a future developer can find the consent setup path.
{%- endcomment -%}
